  "full_report": {
    "title": "FTP server restarts after being turned off and the app is dismissed from recents",
    "observed_behavior": "On the FTP server screen, if the user toggles the FTP server from ON to OFF and then closes the app by dismissing it from recents, the FTP server restarts on its own.",
    "expected_behavior": "After the user turns the FTP server OFF and dismisses the app from recents, the FTP server should stay OFF and not restart on its own.",
    "steps_to_reproduce": "1. Open the app. <aa09f6aef3409759f67d672c9efcbd64d8f3b0ee61cf3e8d197f0539e34430d2>\n2. On the storage permission prompt, tap \"Allow\". <9253ef287211a96261d15d2522d1499f880b411f5e49851b98bae34f3403ab9d>\n3. From the main file list screen, open the navigation drawer. <3abd760d81519f7d0b2fe5daa74c918b40f9496bef2bf776dd7b0d8e95a47b49>\n4. In the navigation drawer, tap \"FTP server\". <ed4ddd149d2da1bda9c6a957048313602988bce3f183bd199efeacece662aeec>\n5. On the FTP server screen, toggle the FTP server from ON to OFF. <5f369cd30bd1e5644d294c31e5ff58277cad40b2633f69cc4105944721df8b1b>\n6. Open the Android recents screen from the FTP server screen. <944abf1e97748f2436418aea5aa65a35e80ea307f807f0264ae85d2c80188e7c>\n7. Dismiss the Files app from recents. <b05234dc13810ef197b494fe9ce3b3d6e6927d53c722ad904f3dc53e425da84c>"
  }
}
